# RUN: printf '$\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEXER
# RUN: printf '# comment' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COMMENT --implicit-check-not=Error
# RUN: printf '(+)\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PAREN
# RUN: printf 'foo(+)\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CALL
# RUN: printf 'def bad(,): 1\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SIGNATURE
# RUN: printf 'def bad(): +\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BODY
# RUN: printf '1 * +\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TERM_RHS
# RUN: printf '1 < +\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COMPARISON_RHS
# RUN: printf -- '-+\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNARY_MINUS_RHS
# RUN: printf '3 foo\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=NAME_TRAILING
# RUN: printf -- '-undefined\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=UNARY_UNDEFINED
# RUN: printf 'x + 1\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BINARY_UNDEFINED
# RUN: printf '1 + undefined\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BINARY_RHS_UNDEFINED
# RUN: printf 'def foo(x): x\nfoo(undefined)\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CALL_ARG_UNDEFINED
# RUN: printf 'def foo(x): x\ndef foo(x): x + 1\n' | %pyxc 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=REDEFINITION

# LEXER: unknown token when expecting an expression
# COMMENT: ready>
# PAREN: unknown token when expecting an expression
# CALL: unknown token when expecting an expression
# SIGNATURE: Expected ')' in function signature
# BODY: unknown token when expecting an expression
# TERM_RHS: unknown token when expecting an expression
# COMPARISON_RHS: unknown token when expecting an expression
# UNARY_MINUS_RHS: unknown token when expecting an expression
# NAME_TRAILING: Unexpected name 'foo'
# UNARY_UNDEFINED: Unknown variable name
# BINARY_UNDEFINED: Unknown variable name
# BINARY_RHS_UNDEFINED: Unknown variable name
# CALL_ARG_UNDEFINED: Unknown variable name
# REDEFINITION: Function cannot be redefined.

# coverage error paths: exercise lexer errors, comments ending at EOF, failed
# expressions inside parentheses and calls, malformed empty parameter lists,
# failed function bodies, a failed right operand for '*'/'/'/'%' (ParseTerm),
# '<' (ParseComparison), and unary '-' (ParseUnaryMinus), a trailing name
# token after a complete top-level expression (FormatTokenForMessage's
# tok_name branch), and codegen-level failures new in this chapter: an
# undefined name used as a unary operand, as a binary operand on both the
# left and right side (BinaryExpressionNode::codegen checks L and R
# separately, so both need their own case), and as a call argument (each is
# a distinct codegen() null-propagation branch even though the printed
# message is the same), plus redefining an already-defined function.

